      "quote": "Finance did the usual exit audit and checked the signatures on some discount slips and complimentary-room slips. That’s done every time a manager leaves."
    },
    {
      "label": "Positive Work Relationships",
      "quote": "Whenever a guest complained, she’d come out and stand between us and them, and at New Year she’d give each of us a red envelope, out of her own pocket."
    },
    {
      "label": "Career Development Opportunities",
      "quote": "She’s gone to Shanghai. The group has opened a new flagship hotel there and asked her to go over as director of front office. It’s a level higher than her old job and the pay is a lot better too."
    },
    {
      "label": "Professional Integrity",
      "quote": "They didn’t find any problems, and the audit findings were posted in the department group chat too."
    },
    {
      "label": "Emotional Connection",
      "quote": "Several people cried and said they’d miss her. Her eyes went red too, and she said if any of us ever went to Shanghai, we had to look her up."
    },
    {
      "label": "Organizational Support",
      "quote": "The new manager started last month. He’s nice too, just still getting to know how things work. Last week he even phoned the former manager specially to ask about some handover matters."
    }
  ],
  "interpretation": "The interviewee highlights the manager’s positive impact, the seamless transition process, and the ongoing support from both the former manager and the organization.",
